  "status_text": "Sixteen possible reports can take 32,768 equally likely keys to keep the odds even. Lean checked a sensor system where one fixed sample must keep all 16 reports equally likely under every allowed sensor rule. In the checked four-bit case, 15 input sites are indispensable. Each of their 32,768 patterns must occur equally often in the sample. That makes 32,768 the smallest positive sample size. Each sensor's adjustment can affect at most two report bits and reads only other sites (L-lib-1099).",
